Fork-free busybox for wasm32-wasi (see wasi-sh ARCHITECTURE.md):

- shell/ash.c: run $(...) and builtin pipelines in-process through the
  __host_pipe-backed in-memory pipes, with subshell isolation built from
  ash's own local-variable machinery; dispatch EVERY applet (not just
  NOFORK-marked ones) through run_nofork_applet() — in-process, no fork.
- libbb/vfork_daemon_rexec.c: before each in-process applet run, zero
  bb_common_bufsiz1 (applets like grep keep their globals there and assume
  a freshly-zeroed process) and clearerr() the shared stdio streams (an
  applet that drained stdin leaves the EOF flag set, which a forked child
  would never leak back to the parent); after it, fflush(stdin) so bytes it
  buffered and never read do not become the next applet's input (`head -1`
  twice used to print l1 then l2).

